<title>NETHERLANDS: ING sets up Philippines life insurance unit.</title>
<headline>ING sets up Philippines life insurance unit.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial services group Internationale Nederlanden Groep NV (ING) said on Thursday it had won a licence to sell life insurance in the Philippines.</p>
<p>The Dutch firm, which includes the Netherlands' largest insurer Nationale-Nederlanden, will set up a new unit called ING Life in the area.</p>
<p>The Manila-based branch is expected to start business by the middle of 1997 and will build up a network of intermediaries.</p>
<p>Earlier today Dutch insurer Aegon said it had been granted permission to start life insurance business in the Philippines. -- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
